title: "Who in NIH's dbGaP can be studied, and under which consent"
abstract: "A census of public dbGaP metadata finds that 55.5% of European-ancestry enrolments sit in studies with a general-research-use consent group, against 43.4% of African American and as little as 31.7% of Latin American enrolments. Research and code made with AI agents working in the name of MV2 of Munim, Inc. Code licensed Apache-2.0; text and data CC BY 4.0 unless a file says otherwise."
